coder › Fixed the Queue so pushed jobs run sequentially.

What changed:
- `src/queue.ts`: replaced the `#pending: Promise<void>[]` + eager `job()` call with a `#tail` promise chain. `push` appends `prev.then(...)` so each job runs only after the previous one settles, in push order, and never synchronously (a `.then` callback always runs as a microtask). The runner `await`s `job()` inside `try/catch`, recording throws in `errors` (wrapping non-`Error` values, same as before) without breaking the chain. `drain` loops on `this.#tail` identity so jobs pushed while draining (including from inside a running job) are also awaited. `push` stays synchronous and returns `void`.
- `src/queue.test.ts`: kept the existing coverage intent and added regression tests for: sequential/no-overlap + push order, no synchronous start inside `push`, `push` returns `undefined`, error recorded + next job still runs, `drain` picks up jobs pushed while draining.

Commits on branch `fix/queue-sequential`:
- `12f80b4 Make Queue run jobs sequentially in push order`
- `a2a8d11 Add regression tests for sequential Queue`

